6. Why Request Reason Exists?

The system needs to understand:

Why are you replenishing?

Different reasons may:

Trigger approvals
Use different SAP order types
Use different stock locations
Route differently
7. Request Reason Concept

The document references:

Application & UI Configuration

which means reasons are configurable.

Although the exact list is not shown in your excerpt, typical Consignment Replenishment reasons are:

Reason	Meaning
Fill Up	Bring stock back to PAR level
Consumption Replenishment	Replace consumed inventory
Surgery Support	Support upcoming surgery
Workshop/Event	Support training event
Buffer Stock	Temporary increase
Emergency Replenishment	Urgent stock need
Limited Release Product	Approved restricted products

Your document specifically gives one example:

Request Type = Short Term Consignment
Request Reason = Fill Up
Reason Code = B01

So Fill Up is definitely one of the configured reasons.

8. What is PAR?

PAR = Periodic Automatic Replenishment

Think of it as:

Target Inventory Level

Example:

Product	PAR
Stent A	10

Hospital currently has:

Current Stock = 4

System suggests:

Order Qty = 6

to reach PAR.

9. PAR Check Workflow

Example:

Product

PAR = 10

Current Stock = 6

User Orders = 4

Result:

Final Stock = 10

Within PAR.

No approval needed.

PAR Exceeded

PAR = 10

Current Stock = 6

User Orders = 10

Result:

Final Stock = 16

PAR exceeded.

System performs:

PAR Validation
16 > 10

Approval required.

10. Why PAR Approval Exists?

To prevent:

Overstocking
Inventory waste
Product expiry
Excessive consignment liability

So:

Above PAR
↓
Approval Required
